# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shire — multi-app environment overview
#
# Shire is a monorepo with three workspaces. They share two secrets and one
# database. This file documents how they connect; each app has its own
# .env.example with the full variable list:
#
#   apps/web/.env.example     — Next.js frontend (owns Postgres, proxies to agent)
#   apps/agent/.env.example   — Mastra agent + matching service
#   packages/shared           — Zod contracts shared by both apps (no env)
#
# Local dev quickstart:
#   1. Copy apps/web/.env.example    -> apps/web/.env    and fill in real values.
#   2. Copy apps/agent/.env.example  -> apps/agent/.env  and fill in real values.
#   3. Run migrations:  npm run db:migrate -w @shire/web
#   4. Start agent:     npm run dev -w @shire/agent   (port 3010)
#   5. Start web:       npm run dev -w @shire/web     (port 3000)
#
# Generate the shared service token ONCE and paste the identical value into
# both apps/web/.env and apps/agent/.env:
#   node -e "console.log('shire_'+require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('hex'))"
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# SHARED — must be IDENTICAL in both apps
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Service token
#    apps/web:   SHIRE_AGENT_SERVICE_TOKEN
#    apps/agent: SHIRE_AGENT_SERVICE_TOKEN
#    The web app sends this as `Bearer <token>` on every proxy request to the
#    agent (/chat, /product-qna, /jobs). The agent validates it with
#    crypto.timingSafeEqual. Mismatched tokens => 401 on every proxy call.
#
# 2. Postgres connection
#    apps/web:   DATABASE_URL              (pooled, runtime)
#                DIRECT_DATABASE_URL       (owner, migrations)
#    apps/agent: SHIRE_AGENT_DATABASE_URL  (defaults to DATABASE_URL)
#    The agent reads candidate/job profiles and writes recommendations to the
#    SAME database. Use the same pooled Neon connection string for both. The
#    agent DB is optional: chat and product-Q&A keep working without it; only
#    job-matching / talent-matching require it.
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATA FLOW
#
#   Browser ──(Privy token)──> apps/web /app/api/*
#        │                            │
#        │                            ├──(service token)──> apps/agent /chat,
#        │                            │                       /product-qna, /jobs
#        │                            │                            │
#        │                            ▼                            ▼
#        │                     Postgres ◄──── reads/writes ─────────┘
#        └──── reads recommendations ◄────┘
#
# Matching pipeline (runs in the agent as a BullMQ job):
#   POST /api/candidate/recommendations/refresh  -> agent job-matching
#   POST /api/recruiter/jobs/[id]/recommendations/refresh -> agent talent-matching
#   Agent: Filter -> Rule Score (skill 40/exp 20/loc 15/salary 10/port 10/risk 5)
#          -> LLM Rerank -> save recommendations (score >= 70, notify >= 85)
#   Web: GET /api/candidate|recruiter/recommendations reads them back.
